WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.302
-This year, our first guest
became a four-time Emmy-winning

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:07.673
actor, director, writer, and
producer all in the same night.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:10.409
He stars in a new film
called "Happiest Season,"

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:13.178
which premieres November 25th
on Hulu.

00:00:13.178 --> 00:00:15.915
Here is Dan Levy. Hey!

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.884
Dan, look at you. Come on.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:18.918
-Hey, Jimmy.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.420
-Hey, this year,
the final season

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.289 line:0%
of "Schitt's Creek" aired,

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:24.958
and you completely
swept the Emmys

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:25.959
and broke all these records.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.260
And I want to tell
everyone watching

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.328
that we're not allowed
to say the name of your show

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:30.797
without seeing the logo.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.665 line:0%
That's why when I say
"Schitt's Creek,"

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.333 line:0%
it pops up every time we say it.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.302
-It'll come somewhere.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.503
-Yeah.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.338
But it's been a little while
since the Emmys,

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:41.807
and I haven't talked to you.
Has that night sunk in yet?

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:43.576
What was it like?

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:46.312
-No, first of all,
it was absolute madness.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:48.047
And, no, it will never sink in.

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:51.784
I don't think any of us, when we
walked into that strange tent

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:54.654
in the backyard
of an event space in Toronto,

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:57.924
really had any indication
of what was going to happen.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.527
We kind of describe it like

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:03.296
you know those kind of, like,
"Host a Murder" board games

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.931
where you invite
a bunch of friends over,

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:07.266
and each of you comes prepared
with, like...

00:01:07.266 --> 00:01:08.500
-Yes.
-...what's your part?

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.372
You're the doctor.
You're the suspicious aunt.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.740
It was like we were being hosted

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.076
at one of those murder
dinner parties,

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:20.446
except we were all
given the character of, like,

00:01:20.446 --> 00:01:22.381
"You're nominated for an award."

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:25.984
And then instead of someone
getting murdered at the dinner,

00:01:25.984 --> 00:01:27.620
we just all got Emmys.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.758
It was, like, the greatest night
of my life.

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.292
-It was great.
And there's even more

00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:34.928
congratulations
in order for you,

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:38.030
because "People's"
Sexiest Man Alive issue

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:41.033
comes out this Friday,
and look who made the list.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.736
Look at this. Come on.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.905
-Yeah.
-Double page spread?

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.574
-[ Laughs ]
-How does that feel?

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:51.077
-The best part about this
is it's, like --

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:53.279
Sure, it's Sexiest Man Alive,

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:56.415
but I get
the "In Quarantine" part.

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:58.484
So there's, like --

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:02.088
There's, like, Michael B.
Jordan, which is much deserved,

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.256
and then I'm kind of the one

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:05.090
that's, like, peeking my head
out of the house

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:09.128
being like, "I've been in here
for 67 straight days!"

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:11.030
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.465
-But, listen.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.700
-No, you --
-A great honor.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:19.005
-I hear that quarantine led you
to discover reality TV.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:22.242
You've never
watched reality TV before?

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.177
-Well, I mean,
I worked in reality --

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:27.212
Before I did the show,
I was working on MTV

00:02:27.212 --> 00:02:29.449
with "The Hills"
for a long time,

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:32.318
a show that
some people might know.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.654
-I love "The Hills."
-And I was doing the aftershow

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.122
for "The Hills."

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:39.325
And when you work so closely
with a reality television show,

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.260
and I loved "The Hills" --
-Yeah, me, too.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.597
-But it kind of takes the magic
out of the experience

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.366
of watching reality television,
'cause you kind of end up

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:49.301
knowing too much
about how it works.

00:02:49.301 --> 00:02:50.603
-Yeah.
-So I had to take,

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:54.072
like, a long hiatus,
and then quarantine happened,

00:02:54.072 --> 00:02:55.341
and I had quite literally

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:58.177
watched every show
on television,

00:02:58.177 --> 00:03:00.313
and so I finally
just resolved myself

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:05.018
to just accepting the fact that
I only have reality TV left.

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:08.654
Not to diminish the genre,
but it started,

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:10.957
and then it became a problem.

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:12.825
-Because it's the best thing
that's ever existed.

00:03:12.825 --> 00:03:14.326
-Well, because I couldn't stop
watching it,

00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:15.929
and now I guess
it's all I watch.

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:18.030
-Yeah. Me, too. What's your jam?

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.298
What are you watching?

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:22.168
-I started with
a "Real Housewives of Atlanta."

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:24.971
I ended with
a "Below Deck Mediterranean."

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.739
-Oh, my God.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.574
That's my jam, "Below Deck."

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:30.810
I'm so -- Captain Sandy?
-Have you caught up, though?

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.811
-Captain Sandy or Captain Lee?

00:03:32.811 --> 00:03:34.647
-Captain Sandy --
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.315
-The drama that happens

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:40.719
on the last season of
"Below Deck Mediterranean" is...

00:03:40.719 --> 00:03:42.621
-It's unbelievable.

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:43.723
-...earth-shattering.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.991
-I'm a Hannah fan,
from way back.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:49.862
-I have many times thought about
vacationing to Australia

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.965
to take Hannah's
yachting course.

00:03:52.965 --> 00:03:54.366
-I'll go with you.
Does she really do that?

00:03:54.366 --> 00:03:55.601
'Cause I will go with you.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.069
We should do that.
-Yeah, that's what she does now.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:00.106
She's teaching a course
on how to be a yachtie.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.641
And I thought --

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.743
Should we go?
-Dude, I will definitely --

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.845
I'm there. Are you kidding me?
-Okay.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.380
-The show is --
The whole drama with Hannah,

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.350
I was like, "What is going on?"

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.520
-I would last 25 seconds
on that ship.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.621
-I can't even.

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:17.190
It was just -- Yeah, I agree.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.691
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.893
-I want to talk
about your new movie.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:22.661
-Yeah.
-It is called "Happiest Season."

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:25.564
It is a great, feel-good
holiday movie.

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:28.534
Kristen Stewart is, you know,
one of my all-times.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.102
I just love her so much, man.

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:32.071
And I love the plot.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.807
I think -- I mean, it just
works, and it's funny.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.475
You want to tell everyone
what it's about?

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:40.713
-Yeah. Well, it's the first
studio lesbian rom-com,

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.348
Christmas rom-com.

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:45.684
So, round of applause
to Clea DuVall,

00:04:45.684 --> 00:04:47.219
who got that one
off of the ground.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:50.956
-Good for Clea DuVall.
-And it's about two women

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:52.558
who are falling in love,

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.394
and Mackenzie Davis' character

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:58.263
invites Kristen Stewart's
character home for the holidays.

00:04:58.263 --> 00:05:00.399
And then just as they're
pulling into the driveway,

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:03.835
we realize that Mackenzie
has not come out to her family

00:05:03.835 --> 00:05:06.171
and that Kristen will have to
sort of go along with

00:05:06.171 --> 00:05:09.775
or not go along with this idea
that they're now going to

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:12.445
play into something that
her parents don't know about.

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:15.581
And I play Kristen's
best friend,

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:18.417
who is not having
any of the mayhem.

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.419
And I think -- Yeah.

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:21.687
-It's super fun.

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:23.422
It's, like, holiday good times.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:24.857
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:24.857 --> 00:05:27.293
Here's Dan Levy
in "Happiest Season."

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:28.594
Take a look at this.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.495
[ Indistinct conversations ]

00:05:30.495 --> 00:05:31.531
-[ Whispering ] Abby.

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:32.765
Abby!
[ Clears throat ]

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.734
Sorry.

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.169
What?

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:38.604
-Um...

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:39.672
How are you here?

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:40.973
-When are you going to get this?

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:43.142
I have been tracking you.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.443
Oh, oh --
[ Clears throat ]

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.478
-Hello.
-Hi.

00:05:46.478 --> 00:05:48.881
-I'm Tipper. This is my home.
-Oh.

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.417
-Are you the ex-boyfriend?

00:05:55.287 --> 00:05:56.489
-[ Clears throat ] Y-Yes.

00:05:56.489 --> 00:06:01.661
I'm...John, Abby's
heterosexual ex-boyfriend,

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:04.197
and I have come to get her back.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:05.865
-Mm, I see.

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:09.435
Well, it would have been nice
to have known you were coming.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:13.005
But since you are here, enjoy.

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.640
-Thank you so much.

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:20.213
Okay, I nailed that,
and she is fabulous.

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.813
-Dan, I'd love to play
a new game with you.

00:06:21.813 --> 00:06:23.448
Would you mind sticking around?

00:06:23.448 --> 00:06:24.517
-Hell yes.

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.085
-More with Dan Levy
after the break!

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.887
Come on back, everybody!

